<title>CHILE: Chile Enami gets $70 mln loan for copper smelters.</title>
<headline>Chile Enami gets $70 mln loan for copper smelters.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile's state mining company Empresa Nacional de Mineria, Enami, said it has received a $70 million syndicated loan to finance a modernization and clean-up plan at its two copper smelters.</p>
<p>The loan is for seven years and was granted with a spread of 31.25 basis points above LIBOR, according to the statement.</p>
<p>The syndicate was headed by France's Societe General and included Japanese and U.S. banks, it said.</p>
<p>Enami is investing $150 million in modernizing and cutting pollution from its ageing Paipote and Ventanas smelters.</p>
<p>((--Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
